# The upstream clone is a build artifact, not source. This single line is the
# load-bearing wire of the whole patch system: because the tree is never
# tracked, a surviving modification to code we did not write is by construction
# a bug — a failed revert, or a hand edit that should have been a patch. The
# tree is regenerated from `upstream commit + patches/` on demand.
upstream/

# tmp/ is a symlink into RAM. Logs, packet captures, measurement runs, build
# scratch — all regenerable, none of it belongs in history.
tmp

# Generated by the monorepo's project initializer, rewritten on every run.
scripts/enter-sandbox.sh

# Compiled server binaries and the staging/live install trees. Derived from the
# clone plus the patch set; rebuilding is the supported way to get them back.
build/
install/

# Extracted client data (DBC tables, map/vmap/mmap collision and pathing files).
# These come out of a copy of the retail client nobody should be redistributing,
# and the custom ones are generated from assets/geometry by our own tools.
assets/extracted/
assets/generated/

# The account and realm the client logs into are the person's own. The example
# is tracked; the filled-in copy stays local.
input/realm
input/account

# A session recording is an output, not a source. Sessions replay from the
# packet log plus the world snapshot, so the renders themselves stay out.
output/sessions/
